1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
An AI that ANSWERS your question and an AI that actually does the TASK? They are not quite the same thing.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Think of a chatbot as someone you can ask for DIRECTIONS. You ask, it explains the ROUTE.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:15,000
An AI AGENT is closer to an
assistant that can use TOOLS.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,000
You might ask it to find a MEETING time. It could check an available calendar, compare slots, and prepare an INVITATION.

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:27,500
The difference is not that one is MAGICALLY intelligent. It is what the SYSTEM is set up to do.

6
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:36,000
A chatbot usually gives you a response. An agent can work through STEPS: plan, use a tool, CHECK the result, then continue.

7
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:43,500
But here is the catch: agents can make MISTAKES, misunderstand a GOAL, or take an action you did not intend.

8
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:48,500
Important actions should have clear
PERMISSIONS and human APPROVAL.

9
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:51,500
A CHATBOT responds. An
agent can take STEPS.

10
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:55,000
So remember: ANSWERS are one
thing; taking STEPS are another.
